    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, led by **Kyle Tucker** (77.80) and **Gunnar Henderson** (74.77). **Kyle Tucker** thrives against McCullers Jr. in a favorable park environment, while **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite matchup against P\u00e9rez and a +2% boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, maximizing his stolen base potential. **Jackson Merrill** (70.37) also anchors our lead-off spot; despite a poor BvP history, the +13% platoon advantage against Houser and his elite lead-off placement make him a core contributor. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.68) remains a must-start despite facing the challenging McClanahan, as his high xwOBA and platoon-neutral efficiency provide a high floor for counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (59.14), who narrowly missed the cut. While his SP skill bonus against Schultz was promising, the optimizer favored **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Miguel Vargas** (61.42) due to superior situational stacking against their respective targets. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) also proved to be a pivotal inclusion; despite lower raw base power, his elite 0.407 xwOBA and prime spot against Ure\u00f1a make him a critical leverage play. Managers should keep a close eye on **Josh Jung** on the bench, as his 45% rain risk combined with a matchup against Warren made him too volatile to bypass our more efficient starters. With **Jacob Wilson** (49.25) catching a slight wind-out bonus in his tilt against Wheeler, the lineup is optimized to prioritize efficiency and volume across all 5x5 categories.",
